# shadcn/ui Component Development

## shadcn/ui Philosophy
- shadcn/ui is a **component collection**, not a library — you own the code (never install as npm package)
- Components are built on **Radix UI** primitives for accessibility and composability
- All components live in your codebase and are fully customizable
- Configuration in [`components.json`](../../components.json) (style: new-york, baseColor: slate, CSS variables enabled)

## Adding shadcn/ui Components

**Always non-interactive** — `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <component> -y -o`. Use `--dry-run`/`--diff` before overwriting customized components. Agent terminals hang on overwrite prompts without these flags.

```bash
# Add a single component (canonical form)
pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add button -y -o

# Add multiple components
pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add button dialog form -y -o

# Preview before overwriting
pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add button --dry-run
pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add button --diff
```

| Flag | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `-y` / `--yes` | Skip general confirmation prompts |
| `-o` / `--overwrite` | Overwrite existing files without prompting |

**When to use `-o`:** installing new primitives or intentionally re-pulling upstream shadcn updates.

**When NOT to use `-o`:** the component in `src/components/ui/` has local customizations — use `--dry-run` or `--diff` first, then merge manually.

**Do not** pipe `yes` into the CLI or run bare `shadcn add` in agent terminals.

Components from any registry other than shadcn's own need review before landing in `src/components/ui/` — `check:no-shadcn-pkg` only blocks npm-package imports; a CLI-vendored file trips no gate.

Components install to `src/components/ui/` with full source code.

## Component Structure
- **Location**: All shadcn components in [`src/components/ui/`](../../src/components/ui/)
- **Imports**: `@/components/ui/[component-name]`
- **Utilities**: `cn()` from `@/utils/tailwind` for className merging
- **Variants**: `class-variance-authority` (cva) for variant management
- **Composition**: Radix UI `Slot` / `asChild` for composition patterns

## Customizing Components
- Edit primitives directly in `src/components/ui/` — follow shipped patterns (e.g. `button.tsx`, `form.tsx`)
- Add variants via cva; extend props by updating the component interface
- Keep accessibility features intact (ARIA attributes, keyboard navigation, `asChild`/`Slot` usage)

## Best Practices
- ✅ Use `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add [component] -y -o` to add components (never bare CLI in agent terminals)
- ✅ Customize components directly in `src/components/ui/`
- ✅ Use `asChild` for composition with Next.js Link and other elements
- ✅ Maintain Radix UI's accessibility features
- ❌ Don't install as npm package (it's copy-paste by design)
- ❌ Don't override accessibility attributes
